1. Use your compiler to generate assembly for each file (other than main.c).
2. Compiler you assembly using the command given below:
	  clang -m32 filename.s main.c
3. Run a.out to test your code. You can manually change the parameter that
you pass to your function in main.c to test different cases.

4. Note that max_n and sum_n call read function in a loop. So enter integer values when you run the code.

5. Regression cases in my_tests (main.c calls func(4)):

   cse_pressure.c: prints 5, 6, 7, 8 twice, then returns 4. Repeated expressions
   remain live across calls after common-subexpression elimination.

   repeated_operand.c: with input 9, prints 1, 1, 1 and returns 4. The results
   of n+n, n*n, and n-n must survive evaluation of the comparison's other side.

   spill_stores.c: prints 5, 6, 7, 8, 99, 100, 104 and returns 4. Spilled loads
   and arithmetic results must survive changes to variables they were stored in.

   Compile and run these C files using steps 1-3 above.
